        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Ephrem the Syrian</strong> <em>Hymns on Paradise</em> <small>(c. 365 AD)</small><p>On &#x27;Let there be light&#x27;, Ephrem distinguishes the first-day light from the fourth-day luminaries: the primordial light is the radiance of God&#x27;s own glory illuminating creation before its instruments (sun, moon, stars) are fashioned. The Ethiopian Andəmta homily extends this by identifying the seven days as a typological prefigurement of the seven ages of salvation history culminating in Christ.</p></aside>',
