        "Easton.",
        "<strong>Dictionary (Easton's).</strong> <strong>PHUT</strong> Phut is placed between Egypt and Canaan in Genesis 10:6, and elsewhere we find the people of Phut described as mercenaries in the armies of Egypt and Tyre (Jeremiah 46:9; Ezekiel 30:5; 27:10). In a fragment of the annuals of Nebuchadrezzar which records his invasion of Egypt, reference is made to “Phut of the Ionians.”",
        "Easton's Illustrated Bible Dictionary, M. G. Easton (1897). Public domain.",
