        "<strong>Dictionary (Easton's).</strong> <strong>NIMROD</strong> firm, a descendant of Cush, the son of Ham. He was the first who claimed to be a “mighty one in the earth.” Babel was the beginning of his kingdom, which he gradually enlarged (Genesis 10:8-10). The “land of Nimrod” (Micah 5:6) is a designation of Assyria or of Shinar, which is a part of it.",
        "Easton's Illustrated Bible Dictionary, M. G. Easton (1897). Public domain.",
