        "Easton.",
        "<strong>Dictionary (Easton's).</strong> <strong>HETH</strong> dread, a descendant of Canaan, and the ancestor of the Hittites (Genesis 10:18; Deuteronomy 7:1), who dwelt in the vicinity of Hebron (Genesis 23:3, 7). The Hittites were a Hamitic race. They are called “the sons of Heth” (Genesis 23:3, 5, 7, 10, 16, 18, 20).",
