        "<strong>Dictionary (Easton's).</strong> <strong>LUD</strong> (1.) The fourth son of Shem (Genesis 10:22; 1 Chronicles 1:17), ancestor of the Lydians probably. (2.) One of the Hamitic tribes descended from Mizraim (Genesis 10:13), a people of Africa (Ezekiel 27:10; 30:5), on the west of Egypt. The people called Lud were noted archers (Isaiah 66:19; comp. Jeremiah 46:9).",
        "Easton's Illustrated Bible Dictionary, M. G. Easton (1897). Public domain.",
