        "<strong>Dictionary (Easton's).</strong> <strong>TIDAL</strong> (in the LXX. called “Thorgal”), styled the “king of nations” (Genesis 14:1-9). Mentioned as Tudkhula on Arioch’s brick (see facing page 139). Goyyim, translated “nations,” is the country called Gutium, east of Tigris and north of Elam.",
        "Easton's Illustrated Bible Dictionary, M. G. Easton (1897). Public domain.",
