        "Easton.",
        "<strong>Dictionary (Easton's).</strong> <strong>ELPARAN</strong> oak of Paran, a place on the edge of the wilderness bordering the territory of the Horites (Genesis 14:6). This was the farthest point to which Chedorlaomer’s expedition extended. It is identified with the modern desert of et-Tih. (See PARAN.)",
        "Easton's Illustrated Bible Dictionary, M. G. Easton (1897). Public domain.",
