        "Easton.",
        "<strong>Dictionary (Easton's).</strong> <strong>COMMUNION</strong> fellowship with God (Genesis 18:17-33; Exodus 33:9-11; Numbers 12:7, 8), between Christ and his people (John 14:23), by the Spirit (2 Corinthians 13:14; Phil. 2:1), of believers with one another (Ephesians 4:1-6). The Lord’s Supper is so called (1 Corinthians 10:16, 17), because in it there is fellowship between Christ and his disciples, and of the disciples with one another.",
