        "Dictionary",
        "Easton.",
        "<strong>Dictionary (Easton's).</strong> <strong>COVERING OF THE EYES</strong> occurs only in Genesis 20:16. In the Revised Version the rendering is “it (i.e., Abimelech’s present of 1,000 pieces of silver to Abraham) is for thee a covering of the eyes.” This has been regarded as an implied advice to Sarah to conform to the custom of married women, and wear a complete veil, covering the eyes as well as the rest of the face.",
