        "Dictionary",
        "Easton.",
        "<strong>Dictionary (Easton's).</strong> <strong>BETHUEL</strong> man of God, or virgin of God, or house of God. (1.) The son of Nahor by Milcah; nephew of Abraham, and father of Rebekah (Genesis 22:22, 23; 24:15, 24, 47). He appears in person only once (24:50). (2.) A southern city of Judah (1 Chronicles 4:30); called also Bethul (Joshua 19:4) and Bethel (12:16; 1 Samuel 30:27).",
        "Easton's Illustrated Bible Dictionary, M. G. Easton (1897). Public domain.",
