        "Witness",
        "MS.",
        '<strong>Manuscript witness.</strong> ilan. "Written in the fifth century, with three columns to the page, and having (what is very unusual in early manuscripts) punctuation, accents, and breathings by the -- original scribe. It contains Gen. 31. 15 Josh. 12. 12, with many losses, however, from mutilation, and small fragments of Isaiah A and Malachi. Its evidence is valuable, and where and B differ it generally agrees with A. G. Codex Sarr',
