        "<strong>Dictionary (Easton's).</strong> <strong>JEGAR-SAHADUTHA</strong> pile of testimony, the Aramaic or Syriac name which Laban gave to the pile of stones erected as a memorial of the covenant between him and Jacob (Genesis 31:47), who, however, called it in Hebrew by an equivalent name, Galeed (q.v.).",
