        "",
        "comm-ethiopian",
        "Tewahedo — Ephrem the Syrian",
        "Ephrem the Syrian (360).",
        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Ephrem the Syrian</strong> <em>Commentary on Genesis</em> <small>(c. 360 AD)</small><p>&#x27;Then Judah came near unto him, and said... let thy servant abide instead of the lad a bondman to my lord&#x27;. Ephrem reads Judah&#x27;s offering of himself as substitute for Benjamin as the OT type of Christ&#x27;s substitutionary atonement: Judah (the tribe of the future Messiah) offers himself FOR another, anticipating the action of his great descendant. Tewahedo Christology preserves this typology as a key OT witness to vicarious atonement.</p></aside>',
        "Ephrem the Syrian, Commentary on Genesis, Section XLIV.18. NPNF Series 2, vol. 13, ed. J. Gwynn / Schaff (1898). PD.",
